{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why","id":1540216,"title":"Underrated Disciplines and Why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-12T13:02:09-07:00","id":1540216,"title":"Underrated Disciplines and Why?","content":"Since we talked about our favorite Disciplines and why. So how about the ones that are not as a popular and has good uses and why you think they are not given there props.<br /> <br /> So here is mine.<br /> <br /> Animalism doesn't seem to get it props in regards to the others, but think about it you have the power to control animals to have a wide spread intelligence network as most would overlook seeing stray dogs, cats, birds and what else hanging about. You have a constant companion if your not much of outgoing person and a quick feeding option. You would have a simple early warning system for your haven and you can transfer your essence into one and get to see daylight and feel almost normal. So that is my idea for a underrated Discipline and I like to hear what you think are underrated Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T20:43:13-07:00","id":1540260,"title":"","content":"Animalism is almost always the top of the list for this for a simple reason: it's the most ST dependent Discipline of the core set. Most of the Disciplines have at least a few reliable powers even if one or two can feel meh if the ST is too heavy handed about things. Animalism can do a ton if you're creative... and your ST is amenable to it.<br /> <br /> IMO most of the other disliked Disciplines aren't underrated... they're just not that great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T12:49:33-07:00","id":1540282,"title":"","content":"I took my sweet time to answer this, yet it's hard to think of any other answer than Animalism.<br /> <br /> To say that not every disliked Discipline are bad, some are disliked because of other reasons instead of being weak, as Vicissitude or Obeah. They're gimmicky, they're situational, they're disliked themes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:36:36-07:00","id":1540290,"title":"","content":"Well I'm glad that you put in thought into your answer and I thought there would others besides Animalism that get ignored by the more sexy or flashy Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T14:31:18-07:00","id":1540297,"title":"","content":"Id say animalism too. The fact it has undergone more changes than most disciplines over the editions suggests the writers knew this. Its such a thematic discipline too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T15:19:42-07:00","id":1540305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540282#post1540282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To say that not every disliked Discipline are bad, some are disliked because of other reasons instead of being weak, as Vicissitude or Obeah. They're gimmicky, they're situational, they're disliked themes...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also hard to disentangle if people dislike the Disciplines themselves, or the design philosophy that result in the huge number of Disciplines over time. Originally the core seven Clans only had Thaumaturgy and Protean as &quot;special&quot; Disciplines outside of the core set. Then the Independent Clans, Sabbat Clans, and Bloodlines all started getting unique Disciplines, and Malkavians swapped to Dementation, etc. A lot of people just didn't like that whole trajectory regardless of the quality of any individual Discipline within the framework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:20:40-07:00","id":1540308,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with animalism is its usefulness. Having an animal partner is attractive and useful to some extent, but the ST can screw up your life and make using this skill very difficult. For example, you can make a pigeon to spy on a conversation, but the ST can only tell you that it doesn't speak human language or read, thus limiting your information. As a combat partner, only in ambushes or against weak opponents, since having a guard dog will only last until it gets shot, which shouldn't be that difficult. In fact, points for V5 in that sense. As food, I've never tried it, but the biggest animal you'll find in the city are large dogs, and unless you can capture them, I don't think it's worth using them as a backup, only perhaps in emergencies. In general, using auspex or domination ends up being more attractive, although it gives some good roleplay opportunities, so is a for fun discipline I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T17:08:45-07:00","id":1540315,"title":"","content":"A suprisingly large numbers of players take auspex for granted despite its solix utilitarian uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T17:16:25-07:00","id":1540316,"title":"","content":"Of course, Animalism lets you deal with more than one animal at a time... and you can ghoul animal companions for boosts (and soaking lethal).<br /> <br /> And large numbers of major urban center still have horses (even if just for police because mounted police have proven to be effective even into the 21st century)... or you know... zoos. Cities also aren't walled off for the most part. Characters can have Domains near parks, or suburban areas where larger animals are either going to be found normally, or can be setup easily enough (ex: start a small beef farm to sell grass fed no antibiotics etc. to fancy restaurants in the city and you've got a large supply of low quality but still usable blood).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T18:29:15-07:00","id":1540319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540315#post1540315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A suprisingly large numbers of players take auspex for granted despite its solix utilitarian uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's surprising indeed, I think all my players have a good respect for Auspex.<br /> <br /> For Animalism, feeding on animals really isn't that hard. Not only are there still big animals in cities, you can always go for numbers. Even the cleanest city is shock full of rats, the classic Nosferatu snack.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the problem ends up being how much you need the ST to be helpful in dealing with animals in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T20:01:18-07:00","id":1540325,"title":"","content":"There's also a serous player/ST knowledge vs. character knowledge gap issue.<br /> <br /> Animals are a lot smarter than a lot of humans give them credit, but we generally don't see it because they have radically different contexts than we do. What makes Animalism feel so underrated is because it bridges that gap: you can tell an animal what you want in a fashion the animal will understand instead of having to spend months or years of training to develop trust and mutual communication with an animal. But there are still limits, and who at the table knows what's reasonable even with Animalism's boost is part of the whole problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T21:41:05-07:00","id":1540328,"title":"","content":"Another aspect of trouble with Animalism is that you often have to keep in mind the difference between humans and animals when it comes to perception and cognitive function. For example, you couldn't tell the dog to follow the guy in the red jacket because of color vision issues, but you can easily have the dog follow their scent. So, the ST has to be aware of the differences to give rulings and the players have to keep aware to choose actions.<br /> <br /> As far as bad disciplines go, I find that often players shy away from the ones that have excessive mechanics associated with it. Potence 5 and Auspex 5 astral projection are leagues apart in mechanics, extra dice rolls, and cost to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T01:55:29-07:00","id":1540333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540319#post1540319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's surprising indeed, I think all my players have a good respect for Auspex.<br /> <br /> For Animalism, feeding on animals really isn't that hard. Not only are there still big animals in cities, you can always go for numbers. Even the cleanest city is shock full of rats, the classic Nosferatu snack.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the problem ends up being how much you need the ST to be helpful in dealing with animals in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its something that's come up a few times in online discussion. Mostly in discussion about disciplines being op, typically clan unique ones. Something i commented on was that auspex is actually a common discipline and is 'better' than most of them with presence, obfuscate and celerity mentioned as well. Several players commented they didnt think it was a very good discipline.<br /> <br /> Could be a newbie error as they also commented they thought celerity was inferior to obtenerbration.<br /> <br /> Edit:thinking on it the quality of a discipline also varies clan to clan due to stuff like discipline overall lineup, clan flaw and culture to use animalism id argue its genrally more useful to gangrel than it is for clan tzmisce and clan nosferatu benifit a lot more from obfuscate than malkavians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-14-2024, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T05:01:22-07:00","id":1540343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540328#post1540328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another aspect of trouble with Animalism is that you often have to keep in mind the difference between humans and animals when it comes to perception and cognitive function. For example, you couldn't tell the dog to follow the guy in the red jacket because of color vision issues, but you can easily have the dog follow their scent. So, the ST has to be aware of the differences to give rulings and the players have to keep aware to choose actions.<br /> <br /> As far as bad disciplines go, I find that often players shy away from the ones that have excessive mechanics associated with it. Potence 5 and Auspex 5 astral projection are leagues apart in mechanics, extra dice rolls, and cost to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>A way around knowing animal's cognitive functions is to interpret the activation roll as framing your need in a way the animal would understand. So the player says &quot;I want the dog to follow that man&quot;, and if enough successes are rolled, the message has been put in a way that the animal understands and can try to execute. After all, we also don't know how Animalism changes the vampire's own cognitive functions, it's probably realistic to say they would intuitively know how to deliver messages to the species they're dealing with.<br /> <br /> As for astral projection, I avoided it as a player because I knew from older players that the ST liked to make it risky, like encountering werewolves or mages. I think VDA20 fixed that, but I have no need to spend 20/28 xp for a power that the ST might turn against me or interpret differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T05:05:04-07:00","id":1540344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540333#post1540333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its something that's come up a few times in online discussion. Mostly in discussion about disciplines being op, typically clan unique ones. Something i commented on was that auspex is actually a common discipline and is 'better' than most of them with presence, obfuscate and celerity mentioned as well. Several players commented they didnt think it was a very good discipline.<br /> <br /> Could be a newbie error as they also commented they thought celerity was inferior to obtenerbration.<br /> <br /> Edit:thinking on it the quality of a discipline also varies clan to clan due to stuff like discipline overall lineup, clan flaw and culture to use animalism id argue its genrally more useful to gangrel than it is for clan tzmisce and clan nosferatu benifit a lot more from obfuscate than malkavians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex's utility may also depend on the table's playstyle. Our ST liked investigative adventures, so high Perception, Alertness, Awareness, Auspex and Eyes of Chaos were super helpful in moving the story forward, even though at some point he changed style slightly because he wanted the players to actually investigate and think and take notes of clues rather than making rolls to uncover things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:20:20-07:00","id":1540401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540315#post1540315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A suprisingly large numbers of players take auspex for granted despite its solix utilitarian uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is shocking as most people I ever played games with have always had a good appreciation for how useful Auspex is for a Kindred to learn as it's a good way to seek out dangers and take steps to avoid it. It's simple survival 101 tactics that most would learn if they want to endure in a dangerous job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:27:15-07:00","id":1540404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540343#post1540343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A way around knowing animal's cognitive functions is to interpret the activation roll as framing your need in a way the animal would understand. So the player says &quot;I want the dog to follow that man&quot;, and if enough successes are rolled, the message has been put in a way that the animal understands and can try to execute. After all, we also don't know how Animalism changes the vampire's own cognitive functions, it's probably realistic to say they would intuitively know how to deliver messages to the species they're dealing with.<br /> <br /> As for astral projection, I avoided it as a player because I knew from older players that the ST liked to make it risky, like encountering werewolves or mages. I think VDA20 fixed that, but I have no need to spend 20/28 xp for a power that the ST might turn against me or interpret differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree about the interpretation of the command. Not only due to how Animalism affects the character, but because it is the character who's giving commands, not the player, and the character's ability to do so is represented by the roll.<br /> <br /> On play style and using the Discipline against the player, though, I think this isn't something specific against Auspex. I've seen STs that interpret extra successes in strength roll as excessive force, for example. Any Discipline can end up being badly interpreted by the ST, and made bad that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T01:59:44-07:00","id":1540420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540401#post1540401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is shocking as most people I ever played games with have always had a good appreciation for how useful Auspex is for a Kindred to learn as it's a good way to seek out dangers and take steps to avoid it. It's simple survival 101 tactics that most would learn if they want to endure in a dangerous job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sonething i clocked a while ago was how differant disciplines are rated relies a lot on your imagination or lack of, i once watched a toreador wreck a lasombra simply because he attacked her in a place with no natural light source. Which rather ironic really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-15-2024, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:30:29-07:00","id":1540460,"title":"","content":"That sounds like bad gameplay Ragged Robin. The darkness is a Lasombra's friend and they would have a major advantage calling upon their signature Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T09:13:27-07:00","id":1540511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540460#post1540460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like bad gameplay Ragged Robin. The darkness is a Lasombra's friend and they would have a major advantage calling upon their signature Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they wouldnt, obtenerbration does not come with darksight, its a specific distinct in clan merit. You can see through your powers but you cant see through darkess in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T21:36:53-07:00","id":1540549,"title":"","content":"Also, don't you need some source of light to generate shadows for certain Obtenebration powers to use? Total darkness would be effectively the same as being surrounded by floodlights in that respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T00:53:42-07:00","id":1540552,"title":"","content":"Random side note, Animalism is also extremely underrated from a Ghoul point of view.<br /> <br /> Since a Ghoul's discipline access is determined by the Generation of their Domitor, when you look at the first dot in every discipline, Feral Whispers is quite a lot of supernatural power for no roll and no blood/WP cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T06:56:06-07:00","id":1540763,"title":"","content":"There are two ways to look at it. One is which discipline gets underrated most often in a vacuum, and that's Animalism for the various reasons on which I don't need to elaborate because they've already been stated.<br /> <br /> The other is which discipline gets underrated in relation to its effective power ceiling; that is to say, players think its power and utility is &quot;here&quot; when it's really &quot;up there&quot; and how great that difference is. That is, by a wide margin, Auspex. Auspex in the right hands is the one discipline to rule them all, and most players seem to think it's &quot;pretty good&quot; to &quot;great&quot; -- usually because they've just never seen it used by someone truly fluent in its use.<br /> <br /> Animalism would easily beat Auspex out in terms of players' perceptions versus reality, rather than just how often it's underestimated at tables. But, as others pointed out, Animalism's power is effectively capped by how generous the ST is allowing players to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T11:43:14-07:00","id":1540794,"title":"","content":"I think Auspex (esp. high dots in Auspex) suffers similarly to Animalism in terms of &quot;player expectations vs. actual ceiling,&quot; because it's also a fairly ST dependent Discipline. What your PC manages to learn from emotional impressions on an object, can skim out of a target's mind, or can find via Astral Projection aren't locked in stone as having to have specific plot-relevant positive impacts. How important what you learn is, is up to whatever answers the ST gives you (esp. if your ST is a stickler for the &quot;reveal things cryptically&quot; stuff).<br /> <br /> The number of times I've run into players that default to Auspex &quot;spam&quot; where they keep using it until they're satisfied they've gotten everything the ST is willing to part with implies most players to realize how much potential the Discipline has... as do enough STs that players feel like they're not being given easy access to those heights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T14:05:06-07:00","id":1540802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540794#post1540794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Auspex (esp. high dots in Auspex) suffers similarly to Animalism in terms of &quot;player expectations vs. actual ceiling,&quot; because it's also a fairly ST dependent Discipline. What your PC manages to learn from emotional impressions on an object, can skim out of a target's mind, or can find via Astral Projection aren't locked in stone as having to have specific plot-relevant positive impacts. How important what you learn is, is up to whatever answers the ST gives you (esp. if your ST is a stickler for the &quot;reveal things cryptically&quot; stuff).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree to a certain extent, but the difference to me is in how ST's interpret and perceive the disciplines, and what incentives and disincentives ST's face through player character use.<br /> <br /> With Auspex, there's a heavy incentive for ST's to be generous with levels 2-4 as it helps prevent derail. It's a quick and easy way for an ST to put their thumb on the scale while making the player feel like they've accomplished something...especially with core book suggestions for Auspex to activate involuntarily at times, and for ST's to roll on players' behalf to keep them from knowing if they've succeeded or by how great a margin.<br /> <br /> Ideally the roll is just there to preserve player suspension of disbelief, and you're feeding them the information they <i>need</i> to connect story beats/plot points regardless of it. Sure it's cheaty, but the utility outweighs the cheatiness. Works best with a Malkavian PC in the coterie, but in a pinch any clan with Auspex does the trick.<br /> <br /> With Animalism, there's a mild disincentive as social scenes with animal servitors (or solo scenes with possession) tend to exclude other players. Sure, that applies for astral projection too, but generally less so -- bare minimum, an ST can play animals in ways that amuse everyone at the table while still being of narrative benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T10:58:36-07:00","id":1540902,"title":"","content":"Maybe a better title would have been underused Disciplines for this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T11:51:15-07:00","id":1540904,"title":"","content":"I think Spiritus is under rated. I know it's confined to a small bloodline, but it's incredibly useful and versatile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T14:11:23-07:00","id":1540909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540902#post1540902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a better title would have been underused Disciplines for this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case the discipline of &quot;Common Sense&quot; would probably top the list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T14:49:13-07:00","id":1540912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540904#post1540904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Spiritus is under rated. I know it's confined to a small bloodline, but it's incredibly useful and versatile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Spiritus itself is underrated, it's the Ahrimanes who seems both hard to include in a game, and don't get much love from players and STs.<br /> <br /> The setting itself is partially to blame as it presents the bloodline always as having been extinct before the start of the game in both its incarnations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T16:36:40-07:00","id":1540919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540909#post1540909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case the discipline of &quot;Common Sense&quot; would probably top the list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The rarest of powers in the world in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T00:06:56-07:00","id":1540956,"title":"","content":"Animalism(V20). Gets slept on and most only take 2 levels for the convenience. <br /> <br /> lvl1 is a toolset. But you have to establish rules/guidelines/expectations with the ST so neither parties get disappointed. So many uses but you kinda need to study what animals can do and how they navigate their environments. Most dogs can scent track well and even tell different blood types, if someone has cancer, or if someone has mated recently. Ravens/Crows recognize individual people and can communicate that info. They can also solve logic puzzles. Rats can chew through about anything given time. there are tons of easy uses a neophyte can use to get boons its silly.<br /> <br /> Sabbat? Hey Tzimisce guy, craft this ordinance into this dog will ya?<br /> <br /> Combat is less efficient but it can be a good assassination tool vs ghouls/regular people. They dont hold up vs most vamps but they deal Lethal. <br /> <br /> Lvl2 is generally seen as 'i need a snack and im outside the city'. True but think how this lets DA vamps travel without needing juicebags in tow. That enemy general on horseback during that night attack? Call him, the horse, over. Summon other messenger animals that other Animalism vamps use - heres your DA interwebs.<br /> <br /> lvl3 is seen as 'crappy Dominate' but thats weak. Great for DA when language barriers are a thing. great for disabling enemy/frienemy ghouls. That love interest of that Toreador isnt so feisty anymore and gets tossed aside. Be a shame if you scooped them up. Ghouls that dont perform well usually dont survive well either. Gang/Mobsters. Chief Accountants, etc. Remember it takes a while for their WP to regenerate.<br /> <br /> lvl4 Others have called this a 'weaker Protean4' but they cant read. lvl4 allows so much it gets stupid once you think about it. Its a launching platform for other disciplines, infiltration, or daytime raids. daytime ops usually needs lots of WP and preferably a few Merits but it can work. racoons are very useful. <br /> <br /> lvl5 can ruin plots. Its that powerful. Risky but powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T07:43:33-07:00","id":1540961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540956#post1540956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animalism(V20). Gets slept on and most only take 2 levels for the convenience...</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking down pre-V5 Animalism by-level, its panoply of powers, and the potential it represents to characters in turn on an individual level pretty much highlights the issues with the discipline, who gets it, and how/why it gets slept on for the most part. All the relevant utility is frontloaded in levels 1-2. Most characters just won't have use cases for higher levels, those use cases come up too rarely to justify the purchase, and/or those levels don't fit within players' plans or the opportunity cost for buying them is just too high (it's experience that could be spent on attributes, skills, or other disciplines with greater utility). The &quot;DA versus modern nights&quot; dichotomy only exacerbates that.<br /> <br /> Level 4 is the best (worst?) example of that in play. Possessing animals is great, but to get the most out of it the character needs a host of social or mental disciplines clans with Animalism tend to not have in-clan...and those who do, have preferable alternatives in-clan (and those alternatives often exist within the boundaries of those disciplines themselves). With the right merits, no place accessible to an animal isn't also accessible to an obfuscated Nosferatu, astral projection is straightforwardly more useful for a Tzimisce, and Gangrel get Protean for crying out loud. Ravnos are the only clan for which animal possession is a premium, simply because they have no other alternatives to do what it does (which coincidentally means their effective use of it is limited).<br /> <br /> Animalism 5 is amazing, but getting the most of it means taking the &quot;short-tempered&quot;/&quot;being a Brujah with ECD&quot; synergy -- that in itself is a major expenditure with a potentially negative risk-reward analysis. Side note, that's one of the minor reasons I've always thought Brujah and Gangrel both would be more interesting if they swapped Animalism and Presence.<br /> <br /> Animalism is great, but past level 2 the question stops being &quot;is this discipline good?&quot; and becomes &quot;are other disciplines better for what I'm trying to do?&quot;. All of this boils down to one thing: designers never seemed able to figure out what they wanted Animalism to be, and left it a bipolar split between control over animals and influence over the Beast (and mortals' animal instinct) where both aspects are partially explored without creating a singular thematic whole.<br /> <br /> That's why I think V5 Animalism represents what's great about V5 mechanics. Players have the agency to explore which thematic side of Animalism they wish, and to a degree of specificity and utility past editions lacked the mechanics to provide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T21:31:01-07:00","id":1540984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540961#post1540961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Breaking down pre-V5 Animalism by-level, its panoply of powers, and the potential it represents to characters in turn on an individual level pretty much highlights the issues with the discipline, who gets it, and how/why it gets slept on for the most part. All the relevant utility is frontloaded in levels 1-2. Most characters just won't have use cases for higher levels, those use cases come up too rarely to justify the purchase, ...<br /> <br /> Level 4 is the best (worst?) example of that in play. Possessing animals is great, but to get the most out of it the character needs a host of social or mental disciplines clans with Animalism tend to not have in-clan...<br /> <br /> <br /> Animalism 5 is amazing, but getting the most of it means taking the &quot;short-tempered&quot;/&quot;being a Brujah with ECD&quot; synergy -- that in itself is a major expenditure with a potentially negative risk-reward analysis. Side note, that's one of the minor reasons I've always thought Brujah and Gangrel both would be more interesting if they swapped Animalism and Presence.<br /> <br /> Animalism is great, but past level 2 the question stops being &quot;is this discipline good?&quot; and becomes &quot;are other disciplines better for what I'm trying to do?&quot;. All of this boils down to one thing: designers never seemed able to figure out what they wanted Animalism to be, and left it a bipolar split between control over animals and influence over the Beast (and mortals' animal instinct) where both aspects are partially explored without creating a singular thematic whole.<br /> <br /> That's why I think V5 Animalism represents what's great about V5 mechanics. Players have the agency to explore which thematic side of Animalism they wish, and to a degree of specificity and utility past editions lacked the mechanics to provide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely disagree.<br /> <br /> Relevant utility and front load cost isnt unique to Animalism. Most Disciplines start to either hyper-specialize after 3 dots or have diminished returns. Dominate3+ has diminished returns and way more cost for dice pools to support it. Presence3 is the sweet spot - 4 is niche and 5 while powerful can be very hamfisted and create enemies upon use. Auspex4 is kinda nice but Auspex5 is super hard to play around and leave the vamp utterly vulnerable in two worlds simultaneously. Fortitude is largely a waste. Celerity4+ is usually overkill. Potence4/5 can be replaced by just buffing STR in most cases. Etc Etc.<br /> <br /> Animalism4 doesnt need other Disciplines for utility. Are the tables you play with not very creative? Animals senses are usually as good if not better than Auspex1. <br /> Animalism4 is one of the 2 Disciplines that allows a vamp (that can stay awake) do daytime OPS. Cheaper than Dominate5 in XP and Dicepool terms. Plus a ST might hit you up for a Humanity check for essentially mind raping a human. Lot less likely for possessing an animal. <br /> <br /> Infiltration. Animalism4 is one of the better ways to infiltrate a Tremere Chantry. And they wont even know it. Does target vamp own a pet? His valued ghouls own pets? If yes, you have a VERY high chance of reading sensitive info, watching passwords typed in, listening to conversations, getting a scent ID to parties at a meeting, <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RbTUTNenvCY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RbTUTNenvCY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RbTUTNenvCY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RbTUTNenvCY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Arson. Racoons have dexterous hands, can carry equipment like snooping devices or ordinance. And can install devices.<br /> <br /> Spying. Average dog can listen in on conversations from outside a building. Possess an owl/crow and lip read. Use a rat or racoon to place air tags/etc on cars. infiltrate a building with a few rats, use them to tap into Routers/etc.<br /> <br /> Scouting. The Sherriff keeps track of all the local animals? No. Not unless high level Animalism use(maybe).<br /> <br /> Sorry, Animalism4 doesnt need other Disciplines and offers utility other Disciplines cant, unless ST lets the Tremere have a 'i win' button with custom Rituals/Paths, which punishes all other Disciplines anyhow. <br /> <br /> Animalism5 doesnt only work on Brujah. Far from it. Animalism5 can alter plots.<br /> <br /> Scenario A, which is more common: Vamp needs to go to Elysium and face witty Toreador Harpies that are gonna ridicule char until Frenzy. Animalism5 users can care less. Because he left his Beast in some poor chained up human down in the warrens. I wonder what happens when the Toreador just CANT rile up said vamp and tables get turned on them? Cool as cucumber vamp ridicules Harpies for failing to insult him. Ghetto Pavis of Foul Presence.<br /> <br /> Scenario B, more rare and requires much planning: ST has a tense deal between 2 unlikely and shaky allies. Their meeting place is know due to good recon. Be a damn shame if during a tense moment of negotiation one of them frenzied, or had to burn lots of WP to keep from frenzy, right? Some Disciplines like Thaumaturgy cost lots of WP. This is a way to weaken an Elder and due to Animalism being so 'useless' may not know what is happening to them. Bonus points if you pull this off on Coterie/Pack mates.<br /> <br /> BONUS: Animalism3 is the more niche level but people conflate it with Dominate or Presence. &quot;Just use Dominate or Presence for the same effect&quot;. Dominate3 offers utility that Dominate and Presence cant. Its not meant to command or make a worshipper. Its utility is is shuts down mortals and it leaves little to no trace. Dominate users can use Dominate to diagnose if another Dominate user dominated someone. Dominate requires a shared language AND shared context for a given task. Must also be used in proximity. Animalism3 leaves no such clue and can be used at some range. Someone charmed by Presence? Ask them who they think is super cool that just walked into their lives. Presence also needs proximity, less so language, but can also create stalkers and people whose obsession with the user can create problems. Need to scare that Guard - well Presence2 isnt very discrete, . Animalism3 is way more discrete. Level3 is likely the weakest level, but it does do things other Disciplines cant.<br /> <br /> Anecdotal scenario played ages ago at one of my tables: my Nos neonate hijacked a gang of gangbangers and bound the leader over a few nights and they didnt even know it. Obfuscate2 + Animalism3 + a thin wire + a good Stealth pool. A few hours a night over a week. Even made friends with their pit bulls. Stole their drugs and cash. The gang members were 'too drugged up' to notice or do anything, basically a normal night for them. Blamed the theft on a rival gang. Started a turf war that disrupted a rival's feeding grounds. Went from Resources0 to Resources3 in about a month of ingame time. Was about to offer a Boon to help 'stop' the gang violence but we lost players. <br /> <br /> Different Player at a different table had a Gangrel that offered a '&quot;escort service&quot; to truck drivers at a certain truck stop. They got Soothed into oblivion but they seemed happy and came back, after they recouped some blood. They didnt get sexytime sadly. They did get to mule some stuff on their trucks sometimes.<br /> <br /> Now for the designers not settling on what they wanted for Animalism. Again, thats not unique to Animalism. Mechanical balance or even coherence was never a strong suite.<br /> <br /> For V5, glad you enjoy it, not my cup of tea. Seems a mash of V20+Requiem with a Dice Mechanic that is too generic for detail, and doesnt flow as well as Minds Eye. Kinda tweened to me and should i ever play it for time i would build a char to exploit the 'win at a cost' rule. Its like, if you dont want a dice system in the way, why even use one, IMO? Diceless systems are available to port if you dont like LARP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T06:16:01-07:00","id":1540989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540984#post1540984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely disagree.<br /> <br /> Relevant utility and front load cost isnt unique to Animalism. Most Disciplines start to either hyper-specialize after 3 dots or have diminished returns...</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the physical disciplines, the progression of which is entirely linear, the issue isn't whether a discipline hyper-specializes after level 2. The issue is how wide a net the discipline power casts for potential and real use cases, as fits each discipline and the chronicle being played. Sure, majesty for example is a social bomb, but it's guaranteed to have more use cases -- and more important use cases -- than drawing out the beast.<br /> <br /> Possession, animal possession, and astral projection all have the same drawback: it leaves the vampire's body torpid and vulnerable, and it's possible if not likely to &quot;get lost&quot; if the spirit's connection to its original (or host) body is severed. Vulnerability can be worked around, but in astral projection's case there are two additional defensive layers in play: whether the projecting vampire can be detected (which can only happen by supernatural means), and if so, knowledge <i>and</i> ability to affect the projection (again, only by supernatural means). In some cases, a projecting vampire can be <i>more</i> powerful than their default state simply on the back of substituting mental attributes for physical in astral combat.<br /> <br /> They're different risk profiles for different use cases, and ultimately it's down to which best fits the character in question and the chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Animalism4 doesnt need other Disciplines for utility. </div> </div> </div>This isn't about need, it's about how to maximize the power's utility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Infiltration. Animalism4 is one of the better ways to infiltrate a Tremere Chantry... </div> </div> </div>Lest we forget, the Tremere clan's greatest enemies are clans with Animalism, and the clan has Auspex for supernatural senses in-clan as well as Thaumaturgy for its wealth of alarm, detection, banning, and warding rituals. This is a battle they've fought for a thousand years in a quite literal sense, and as consequence have a perpetual siege mentality with paranoia to rival Malkavians' and operational security to rival Nosferatus'. This is probably the single worst idea a Nosferatu, Tzimisce, or Gangrel could conjure to get information on a chantry (provided the ST knows their metaplot basics, anyhow).<br /> <br /> Any other clan except for the Nosferatu and Tzimisce, and it's a great use case, I'll grant that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Sorry, Animalism4 doesnt need other Disciplines and offers utility other Disciplines cant, unless ST lets the Tremere have a 'i win' button with custom Rituals/Paths, which punishes all other Disciplines anyhow. </div> </div> </div>Tremere have so many &quot;I win&quot; options with published rituals and paths for defending havens and chantries, they don't need custom anything. Been there, done that as a player, when I had a PC who worked up to Regent, and later Lord, and had to plan chantries' defenses with my ST. That was a TC game played through during the height of the Omen War, and for all intents and purposes it may as well have been a sidebar tabletop strategy game played parallel to the actual chronicle itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Animalism5 doesnt only work on Brujah. Far from it. Animalism5 can alter plots. </div> </div> </div>Again, this isn't about necessity, it's about maximizing the number of use cases, the likelihood of those use cases' success, and the impact of those use cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T15:47:02-07:00","id":1541007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1540989#post1540989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This isn't about need, it's about how to maximize the power's utility.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very weak argument. What do you even mean by that? All and every power needs other powers and contrived circumstances to work at maximum potential, it just isn't as obvious for others.<br /> <br /> We can just as well say that Animalism is so good that on top of all its normal uses, it can amplify the uses of other Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Animalism is a useful Discipline by itself. It doesn't need any other to be useful, and all its powers are useful in the hands of a creative user. And that's all that matters, because the thread isn't about the most powerful Discipline, it's about the underrated ones. No one said it is the best option of all.<br /> <br /> You could have engaged with the thread with V5 powers or Disciplines you think to be underrated, too, instead you tried to use Animalism as a means to edition warrying. Why was that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T18:36:11-07:00","id":1541011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541007#post1541007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a very weak argument. What do you even mean by that? All and every power needs other powers and contrived circumstances to work at maximum potential, it just isn't as obvious for others.<br /> <br /> We can just as well say that Animalism is so good that on top of all its normal uses, it can amplify the uses of other Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Animalism is a useful Discipline by itself. It doesn't need any other to be useful, and all its powers are useful in the hands of a creative user. And that's all that matters, because the thread isn't about the most powerful Discipline, it's about the underrated ones. No one said it is the best option of all.<br /> <br /> You could have engaged with the thread with V5 powers or Disciplines you think to be underrated, too, instead you tried to use Animalism as a means to edition warrying. Why was that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally said a page ago I felt Animalism was underrated for what it is, and that it's biggest limitation is ST reluctance to explore full freedom of use from both a game balance and player attention perspective. This can be true at the same time as saying it's still limited in use cases compared to alternatives, and the opportunity cost for purchasing it can be prohibitively high, depending on the character concept and chronicle being run. And it can <i>definitely</i> be true in criticizing it from a thematic perspective, because the thematic perspective <i>is</i> what causes many of the issues in the first place.<br /> <br /> In fact, the two go hand-in-hand. It's underrated because ST's arbitrarily restrict its use for one reason or another...but on the other hand, you don't believe the ability to run a table with Animalism <i>may</i> be why ST's restrict its use? It's telling this conversation is about Animalism, as opposed to Vicissitude, Obtenebration, or any of the various blood sorceries, all of which suffer from the &quot;player with it can run the table given unrestricted use&quot; problem equally.<br /> <br /> The issue is not that it amplifies the use of other disciplines, it's that other disciplines amplifies <i>Animalism's</i> use -- and the disciplines which do, are not readily accessible to the clans with Animalism in the same way they are to clans with Dominate and/or Auspex. That's not a predictable influencer on cost-benefit analysis, because as I said, it's dependent on the chronicle and storyteller. You needn't look further than the distinction between dark ages and modern nights settings to see how Animalism's utility is setting-, chronicle-, and storyteller-dependent.<br /> <br /> It's not edition-warring to simply point out V5 mechanics do disciplines like Animalism right, thanks to allowing multiple themes in a single discipline room to breathe. This is a complex topic, and it can't be broken down into &quot;this must be good because the other is bad&quot; logic. Honestly, I think some folks here are starting to get a little reactionary, losing senses of objectivity, and forgetting one or both can be praised as well as criticized, without endorsing or rejecting the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-25-2024, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T03:28:12-07:00","id":1541017,"title":"","content":"How, exactly, does V5 Animalism address the core issue of the &quot;animal control&quot; side of the Discipline still being intensely vague in what it can really accomplish and being very dependent on ST discretion (plus the rather ridiculously high Difficulties given in the examples doesn't really let players cut loose with creative applications of the powers)?<br /> <br /> Being able to choose between &quot;master of animals,&quot; and &quot;master of the metaphorical animal within human-like beings&quot; is nice, but it then mechanically constrained by the fact that you can't really effectively pick both because of V5's &quot;five powers per Discipline period&quot; issue. It also causes filler where now you have to buy Animalsm to have an animal ghoul where you didn't in past editions (and you can only have one), and a minor boost to feeding off of animals longer that does as much to muddy the themes of the Discipline than it does to give it more &quot;breathing room.&quot; It just comes off as trying hard to pad out 9 core powers + Amalgams.<br /> <br /> The reason it comes off as edition warring is that you're not talking about something V5 does to make Animalism less subject to the reasons people consider it underrated, you're using this as an excuse to say that V5's overall design approach is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T10:27:08-07:00","id":1541026,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Theodrim;n1540989]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than the physical disciplines, the progression of which is entirely linear, the issue isn't whether a discipline hyper-specializes after level 2. The issue is how wide a net the discipline power casts for potential and real use cases, as fits each discipline and the chronicle being played. Sure, majesty for example is a social bomb, but it's guaranteed to have more use cases -- and more important use cases -- than drawing out the beast. </div> </div> </div>Not sure that is true on average. Just how broad can Presence5 usage be? Seems like lvl1 and 3 would get the most use and 5 can risk the Masquerade. Settle a whole crowd to the point they stop and kneel before the User? Enforce/reinforce Rule over a meeting? Stifle mass combat(though V20 humans can resist w/WP roll... and ive witnessed STs allow combat hardened soldiers/focused professionals shrug off Presence because they arent beholden to their own emotions -mileage may vary on implementation of that aspect but its in the rules.) Drain a vamp's WP via forcing them to resist Presence, though the lower levels can do that as well at a recurring cost.<br /> <br /> Compare to:<br /> <br /> Auspex5: pretty broad in scope but comes with risk and if ST has exposure to other crossover splats, the vamp loses safety quickly and things can get...surreal. Up to how cute the ST wants to get but an Astral vamp is nothing vs a Mage with similar abilities. Again, just how often would a vamp(non-Malkavian?) use Auspex5? Doesnt it get quit expensive in terms of WP use?<br /> <br /> Dominate5: Now after possessing a human the uses can vary greatly, but it takes quite a bit of setup. How often is it getting used?<br /> <br /> Obfuscate: simple to use and hiding a group has lots of uses. Little cost with mild risk if beneficiaries arent skilled in stealth<br /> <br /> Protean: turning to a cloud has a few potent uses, but i dont think is broadly useful.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy and Necromancy would be hard to guage due to many edge cases.<br /> <br /> Signature disciplines get a bit gimmicky. <br /> <br /> The basic Disciplines at higher levels seem more powerful but more niche to me, IMO. The average char is gonna use lower levels more often than level4/5 in my experience. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possession, animal possession, and astral projection all have the same drawback: it leaves the vampire's body torpid and vulnerable, ... </div> </div> </div>See above, but if St wants to use other splat material, good luck astral vamp.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't about need, it's about how to maximize the power's utility. </div> </div> </div>Sure, and player creativity, but on average, in my experience, PCs and NPCs tend to use lower level disciplines for more situations than lvl5 powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lest we forget, the Tremere clan's greatest enemies are clans with Animalism, and the clan has Auspex for supernatural senses in-clan as well as Thaumaturgy for its wealth of alarm, detection, banning, and warding rituals. This is a battle they've fought for a thousand years in a quite literal sense, and as consequence have a perpetual siege mentality with paranoia to rival Malkavians' and operational security to rival Nosferatus'. This is probably the single worst idea a Nosferatu, Tzimisce, or Gangrel could conjure to get information on a chantry (provided the ST knows their metaplot basics, anyhow).<br /> <br /> Any other clan except for the Nosferatu and Tzimisce, and it's a great use case, I'll grant that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tremere have so many &quot;I win&quot; options with published rituals and paths for defending havens and chantries, they don't need custom anything. Been there, done that as a player, when I had a PC who worked up to Regent, and later Lord, and had to plan chantries' defenses with my ST. That was a TC game played through during the height of the Omen War, and for all intents and purposes it may as well have been a sidebar tabletop strategy game played parallel to the actual chronicle itself. </div> </div> </div>Tremere are the new kids on the block and were able to wrest some power, which is impressive. Their existence is a fraction of duration compared to the other clans, and if you include the V5 metaplot/lore, the Tremere suffered a major blow: their magic didnt protect them and the central leadership/strong blood fell. Missiles &gt; Wards/Clairvoyance/Barries/Demons it seems. Their story is one of Hubris, Desperation, and Pride. Its great! Note: im not anti-Tremere, before accusations fly, but they are one of the Mary Sue clans that can get plot armor from bad STs along with the Ventrue and Toreador. And if i could, i would play a Dominate/Path of Blood Face Tremere. I want to iterate i enjoy the Tremere, im not a hater, but...<br /> <br /> Now, i know a decent amount about the Tremere at the Core rules level and core Lore. There could be some splat/expansion book that gives them hard counters to what i present but i havent seen them yet/dont remember after 20+ years.<br /> <br /> Wards and Circles dont effect non-ghoul animals. Have yet to see a Ward vs Animal. Wards/Circles need to be touched to take effect. Critters can get in and out of chantries just like any other structure. And with some critters, you can listen to conversations without even entering the building. Others can watch who enters and leaves from a literal mile away. Now, stealing a book from the library may be pretty damn difficult, sure. But eaves dropping the chantry is easier than most could imagine.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Clanbook(Revised?) stated Auspex does not detect animal possession. I dont know of any cases of Auspex explicitly detecting and identifying an animal sent to spy with Animalism1. If it was a ghouled animal, sure.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy requires a lot of blood to use, and i would argue including in learning and practice. NAPKIN MATH(just to illustrate a point, not that most tables track this level of detail) Each vamp needs 1BP to rise each night, which is 365 BP per year which is about 37 humans worth of vitae per Tremere. Thats if you drain them dry. So if at minus -4 BP a human's life is at risk, then a lot more vessels will be needed(x3 to x4 more?) just to fuel the vamps in the chantry - thats before any discipline costs/healing/thaumaturgy practice, without sending a conga-line of corpses to the morgue. Rational but ballpark guess, a given chantry may use up to x10 more vitae than other vamp groups and its concentrated in usually one location - That Castle of a chantry may end up being a prison in logistical terms. All that vitae flows to one spot to get used. This allows the patient and perceptive Animalism user to track the flow of humans and blood in the chantry, and very likely corpses out of(sometimes into?) the chantry. Blood and cadaver tracking with dogs is a thing in forensics.<br /> <br /> Related above - Tremere also like Blood Cults. Some of those members surely have pets. Each additional human and ghoul that get access to the chantry, or contact with a Tremere, is another vector for access. <br /> <br /> Tremere tend to rely on human ghouls, which are easily tracked with animals even during the day. Those ghouls wont really have much by way of countermeasures.<br /> <br /> Few Tremere invest in Auspex over Thaumaturgy. Everyone acts like every Tremere has Auspex5. Thaumaturgy is an expensive investment in XP. Auspex as a counter to Obfuscate is <i>overstated</i> with the Tremere - they have WAY too many other things to invest XP in, unless ST wants to give them unlimited XP, time to obtain it, or a slew specialized Elders for each chantry. Animalism clans are more likely to invest in Animalism to a higher degree on average cost alone than the average Tremere into Auspex. Related - a given chantry also wont likely have access to all the Paths like most assume in whiteroom examples.<br /> <br /> I could go on, but Tremere have excellent defense vs magic, strong defense vs regular intruders, and lacking defense vs animals. And none vs missiles, lol. <br /> <br /> Attacking a chantry with Animalism is similar. When you pick it apart, they dont have many defenses. Especially during the day like most other vamps. With planning and setup, arson is quite easy. <br /> <br /> And even in individual combat, Animalism helps vs Tremere. A pack of dogs trained to hunt in a pack with one of them(or more) trained to restrain a target(like a police dog) can easily shut down a Tremere with no support. Grappling hard counters Thaumaturgy, and dog bites do lethal. That vamp likely isnt outrunning them either. Setup would be an ambush, because the system mechanics favor it. <br /> <br /> The other main weakness to Animalism the Tremere have is very up to ST interpretation of Frenzy. Do Tremere keep the ability to use Thaumaturgy while frenzied? And if able to use during frenzy, do they keep enough higher cognitive function to keep from targeting allies or choosing which paths to use and when??? IMO, frenzy overpowers the higher mind needed to use Thaumaturgy. Opinions vary.<br /> <br /> Because Animalism5 can turn that Tremere Elder into a wild artillery platform that is causing havoc and likely all parties will try to put him down asap. <br /> <br /> And, Tremere arent the bastion of power as claimed. If they were they wouldnt have needed Camarilla membership and the Sabbat Tremere would have been under control. They have great mystical utility, and are powerful if given protection and ample resources. But their image portrays more strength than they actually have.<br /> <br /> Apologies if long winded.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T10:35:53-07:00","id":1541027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541017#post1541017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How, exactly, does V5 Animalism address the core issue of the &quot;animal control&quot; side of the Discipline still being intensely vague in what it can really accomplish and being very dependent on ST discretion (plus the rather ridiculously high Difficulties given in the examples doesn't really let players cut loose with creative applications of the powers)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agree.<br /> <br /> V5 Dice pools are prohibitive if a char is gonna lean on a particular pool they need, what 8+ dice to regularly be proficient vs higher difficulties? That pool is hard to get for a new char and expensive if bought with XP. Plus V20 the dicepools for the Animalism powers were most Manipulation-based. Compare to Dominate which is all over the place. A new char in V20 could start with Discipline lvl4 and(usually) have the dicepool to use it well. Moreso with Sabbat. I remember that wasnt really possible in V5 but i could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Plus, doesnt each power lvl2+ require a hunger check? One of the benefits of Animalism in V20 is Animalism is cheap to use, no BP or WP needed in all but a few cases.<br /> <br /> And from what i recall, V5 leaned quite a bit on Requiem re Animalism, which i like. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T13:52:12-07:00","id":1541032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541027#post1541027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 Dice pools are prohibitive if a char is gonna lean on a particular pool they need, what 8+ dice to regularly be proficient vs higher difficulties? That pool is hard to get for a new char and expensive if bought with XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit of a mixed bag.<br /> <br /> V5 Discipline activation pools generally use an Attribute + Discipline rating rather than a Skill. While Disciplines aren't cheap in V5 (char gen or with XP), you have less overall traits you have to invest in to get as good as you can with them.<br /> <br /> What dice pool you &quot;need&quot; depends entirely on what you define as &quot;regularly be proficient,&quot; and how liberal your ST is with taking half when it comes to activating Disciplines If you want to start with a famulus* dog, Manipulation 3, and Animalism 3, you can do so and if your ST is generous with taking half, you can use Feral Whispers to give the dog basic commands without fuss (and way less Rouse checks). If you want to make a vampire that rides horses, you can at least turn one into a famulus, but you're no better at commanding it than any mortal that's your equal in dealing with animals (since as a herbivore the lowest diff to use Feral Whispers is going to be 4 and thus fail a lot since you can't start with Manipulation + Animalism 8+ in V5 default creation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, doesnt each power lvl2+ require a hunger check? </div> </div> </div>No, thankfully, as Animal Succulence would be completely worthless if you had to make Rouse checks to feed off of animals for a bit longer than normal as your Blood Potency increases. That said, V5 Animalism is rather Rouse heavy with only two core powers that don't require checks. Though the three checks to use Bond Famulus last until the animal dies, and negates the Rouse checks of two of the higher level powers you're going to want to use on them a lot; so it's a large net savings for your one close animal companion compared to ordering around random creatures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And from what i recall, V5 leaned quite a bit on Requiem re Animalism, which i like. </div> </div> </div>Not really? As far as I can tell the Bond Famulus power is the only one that seems inspired by Requiem directly instead of being a power VtM and VtR have both used at some point previously. Though I think most people would prefer the VtR 2e version of that power over the V5 version given the respective contexts (esp. given the point of the thread VtR 2e's Raise the Familiar explicitly makes that animal as intelligent as an Intelligence 1 human when it comes to understanding orders given, cutting through a lot of the &quot;what can it do exactly?&quot; issues discussed in the thread even if VtR 2e Animalism in general doesn't fully get rid of that problem either).<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> * - A small peeve, but famulus is a Latin word for a human slave or servant. It has never meant an occult servant, let alone an animal one, which is a multi-step linguistic evolution that happened after the word familiar came into use (originally with its old Latin implications before being applied to occult matters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T18:14:55-07:00","id":1541044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541017#post1541017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How, exactly, does V5 Animalism address the core issue of the &quot;animal control&quot; side of the Discipline still being intensely vague in what it can really accomplish and being very dependent on ST discretion (plus the rather ridiculously high Difficulties given in the examples doesn't really let players cut loose with creative applications of the powers)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dice pools are lower and difficulties are higher across the board; that's not unique to Animalism. It's also counter-balanced by being able to blood buff <i>any</i> roll tied to an attribute as opposed to just physical -- discipline activation rolls included -- as well as getting more statistical mileage out of Willpower expenditure than in past editions.<br /> <br /> As far as what V5 does with regards to &quot;animal control&quot;, well, the very fact there are powers for every level which are still more specific than what past editions have to offer speaks for itself. As well as two subtracks for specializing in a famulus as well as controlling animals in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...you can't really effectively pick both because of V5's &quot;five powers per Discipline period&quot; issue... </div> </div> </div>Again, that's not unique to Animalism. It's more available choices to do what's most relevant to the character, the themes the PC wants to explore, and what offers the most utility within those confines. If I'm bringing a Nosferatu PC to the table and what I want to do with that character is doolittling, I now have <i>five</i> levels' worth of powers to do that thing as opposed to a first, second, and fourth. It's building a character around a single holistic concept, as opposed to buying a hodgepodge of predetermined powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...It also causes filler where now you have to buy Animalsm to have an animal ghoul where you didn't in past editions (and you can only have one), and a minor boost to feeding off of animals longer that does as much to muddy the themes of the Discipline than it does to give it more &quot;breathing room.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You actually don't have to buy Animalism to have an animal ghoul, although it certainly helps wrangling ghouled animals that aren't famuli. You can still ghoul animals without the discipline (or the power), the corebook makes that quite clear in the section on ghouls. A famulus just happens to be a ghoul with additional bonuses, which doesn't count against the number of active blood bonds. And since I know it'll come up, you can ghoul a human or animal without blood bonding them.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure what your issue with Animal Succulence is, here. It was in past editions, as a level <i>six</i> power (and weaker comparatively than it is in V5, to boot). If you want to talk about inconsistent design goals, padding, and poor game balance...well, there it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason it comes off as edition warring is that you're not talking about something V5 does to make Animalism less subject to the reasons people consider it underrated, you're using this as an excuse to say that V5's overall design approach is better. </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying this is an example in which V5's overall design approach shines. This <i>does</i> make Animalism less subject to being considered underrated, because it solves for the root issue with Animalism itself: it's a hodgepodge of two themes which don't coexist well, and as a result the discipline has to do too much with each individual level. That's what makes it so inconsistent across tables. Or to put it another way,<br /> <br /> 1. One discipline has to explore two separate and distinct themes over the scope of five powers.<br /> 2. Having to explore those themes over the scope of five powers means individual levels must be open-ended.<br /> 3. The discipline's open-endedness makes it highly subject to ST fiat.<br /> 4. Being highly subject to ST fiat makes it inconsistent across tables.<br /> 5. Its inconsistency across tables leads to players writing it off, because they can't know what to expect from it without a conversation with the ST and experiencing play with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T22:38:30-07:00","id":1541053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541044#post1541044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dice pools are lower and difficulties are higher across the board; that's not unique to Animalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps,but it's sufficiently off-putting compared to Dominate which is either unrolled (usually if you catch a mortal off guard) or resisted rather than having inherently high Difficulties.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the case the Animalism isn't underrated in V5, feel free, but you're argument still goes back to, &quot;V5 Animalism is the best Animalism.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as what V5 does with regards to &quot;animal control&quot;, well, the very fact there are powers for every level which are still more specific than what past editions have to offer speaks for itself. As well as two subtracks for specializing in a famulus as well as controlling animals in general. </div> </div> </div>Except there aren't powers at every level. At best there's four core powers if you include Bond Famulus (which doesn't by itself get you much until you get Feral Whispers, and really has no reason to exist besides filler instead of just making it easier to use Animalism on your animal ghouls as a default rule). Mucking with The Beast only gets three core powers. Though I admit I haven't kept up with V5 much, so it's possible some supplements have fixed some of this by now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, that's not unique to Animalism.... </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Animalsm is both a strong concept, but not really a full 5 powers concept. The fact that even in V5 you're going to end up branching out of &quot;control animals&quot; into other powers or stop investing in Animalism. That factors into its underrating and thus it is specific on Animalism and if V5 really &quot;fixed&quot; it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can still ghoul animals without the discipline (or the power), the corebook makes that quite clear in the section on ghouls. </div> </div> </div>I don't own it, but I distinctly remember that animal ghouls are not mentioned at all in V5 core's Retainers entry or Ghouls entry. Feel free to quote the text if that's incorrect, but the lack of it when I read it the first time around stood out that I remember its absence even now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not entirely sure what your issue with Animal Succulence is, here. It was in past editions, as a level <i>six</i> power (and weaker comparatively than it is in V5, to boot). If you want to talk about inconsistent design goals, padding, and poor game balance...well, there it is. </div> </div> </div>V5 Animal Succulence loses is primary utility at Blood Potency 4 (the +1 Hunger slated is nulled by your feeding getting halved). After that it becomes an extremely niche power that lets you kill your famulus for a once off boost and thus you have to start over with a new one.<br /> <br /> V20 Animal Succulence is useful to any vampire that can get it (you double blood point gains from animal blood at the cost of having to struggle more to resist feeding from humans). Is it worth 6 dots? Not at all. But Elder Disciplines were niche design expanded well beyond intentions into being a mess. I don't recall saying V20's version was good before pointing out that it's enduring viability vs V5's version becoming virtually obsolete until right now though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I'm saying this is an example in which V5's overall design approach shines. </div> </div> </div>That's just putting positive spin on the same action. You're still not addressing things like &quot;Animalism is extremely dependent on ST fiat so players underrate it.&quot; It's just doubling down on, &quot;V5 is objectively the best RPG ever made and I need to yell at people that blaspheme for disagreeing&quot; that seems to be your only goal in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This <i>does</i> make Animalism less subject to being considered underrated, because it solves for the root issue with Animalism itself: it's a hodgepodge of two themes which don't coexist well, and as a result the discipline has to do too much with each individual level. </div> </div> </div>Except that's not what people cite when they ID Animalism as underrated. Serpentis is an utter hodgepodge of powers, but people don't considered it underrated because it gets you a lot of good powers in it's incoherent platter.<br /> <br /> We're on page 3. The clear theme is that Animalism's' root issue is that it's too vague and thus players don't trust it to work in the hands of ST fiat. Which no edition of VtM (or VtR) has addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T06:38:15-07:00","id":1541058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541053#post1541053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps,but it's sufficiently off-putting compared to Dominate which is either unrolled (usually if you catch a mortal off guard) or resisted rather than having inherently high Difficulties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh...what?<br /> <br /> First edition to V20 Dominate has a set target number equal to target's Willpower (permanent pre-V20, temporary in V20). Mortals that aren't major characters have Willpowers of 1-3, mortals that are tend to have Willpowers 3-5. It's generally supernaturals that get Willpower 6+, and of those, it's generally Willpower eight or higher. It's the exact same scenario in practice, other than that pre-V5 mechanics have rules for auto-success too (dice pool higher than target number) and players tend to forget about them.<br /> <br /> Animalism has always just had set difficulties pegged to the type of animal being targeted, the difference is in that players can optimize for Animalism by jacking the Animal Ken skill into the stratosphere at character generation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I admit I haven't kept up with V5 much, so it's possible some supplements have fixed some of this by now. </div> </div> </div>Very much so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't own it, but I distinctly remember that animal ghouls are not mentioned at all in V5 core's Retainers entry or Ghouls entry. Feel free to quote the text if that's incorrect, but the lack of it when I read it the first time around stood out that I remember its absence even now. </div> </div> </div>Because God forbid a White Wolf product ever have sensible formatting or indexing, it's on page 234 under the blood bond. Don't ask me why it's there and not the actually relevant sections, why those sections don't at least include page references, or why there isn't a page reference in the index, I haven't the foggiest idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 Animal Succulence loses is primary utility at Blood Potency 4 (the +1 Hunger slated is nulled by your feeding getting halved). After that it becomes an extremely niche power that lets you kill your famulus for a once off boost and thus you have to start over with a new one. </div> </div> </div>That's down to how you interpret the power, thanks to how strangely it's written. The plain-text is clear the bonus is additive so order-of-operations matters, namely whether the additional Hunger is accounted before or after the blood potency coefficient. That is to say, (XY)+1 or (X+1)Y -- where X is the amount of Hunger slaked from the animal(s) and Y is the blood potency coefficient.<br /> <br /> There's no specific rule overriding BEDMAS, as is the case with the Fortitude power Toughness. Therefore, I interpret the additional Hunger is slaked <i>after</i> the blood potency coefficient. In turn, that means a vampire with the power can always slake at least one Hunger from animals regardless of blood potency. Which is fair enough, and well within the purview of a level-3 discipline power in V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to make the case the Animalism isn't underrated in V5, feel free, but you're argument still goes back to, &quot;V5 Animalism is the best Animalism&quot;...That's just putting positive spin on the same action. You're still not addressing things like &quot;Animalism is extremely dependent on ST fiat so players underrate it.&quot; It's just doubling down on, &quot;V5 is objectively the best RPG ever made and I need to yell at people that blaspheme for disagreeing&quot; that seems to be your only goal in this thread. </div> </div> </div>Now you're just putting words in my mouth. We're now from &quot;V5 did this thing right&quot; to &quot;V5 is the best edition&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that's not what people cite when they ID Animalism as underrated. Serpentis is an utter hodgepodge of powers, but people don't considered it underrated because it gets you a lot of good powers in it's incoherent platter. </div> </div> </div>People don't consider Serpentis overrated because it provides a lot of <i>overpowered</i> abilities that are capable of replacing entire disciplines, if not being straightforwardly more powerful than entire discipline <i>lines</i>, in a pinch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're on page 3. The clear theme is that Animalism's' root issue is that it's too vague and thus players don't trust it to work in the hands of ST fiat. Which no edition of VtM (or VtR) has addressed. </div> </div> </div>If nobody disagrees with that -- and it doesn't seem like anyone is -- why is it a bone of contention? Again, I think people are letting general disdain for V5 get the best of them and are being oversensitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T13:02:00-07:00","id":1541077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541058#post1541058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh...what?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're responding to a line of discussion about your claim than V5 Animalism isn't unique in things like having low dice-pools and high difficulties. So I contrasted it with V5 Dominate. For someone that keeps banging on about how great V5 is, you'd think you could recognize something a distinct as V5's whole, &quot;No roll is required against an unprepared mortal,&quot; caveat present in a number of V5 Dominate powers as being unique to V5 and thus not about V20.<br /> <br /> [quote[Very much so.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Such as? All I can find is a supplement added one core power (on the Beast manipulation side of things) and a few more amalgams. That doesn't seem like a &quot;very much so&quot; situation as that still leaves each of the Disciplines thematic strands at 4 powers without Amalgams, forcing characters without access to an appropriate Amalgam to branch away from their theme of focus... thus not really changing the end result of pre-V5 Animalism even if reducing it a bit (and I'm discounting Amalgams because Combo Disciplines are a thing in pre-V5 that allow for unlimited need powers to buy it you want to hyper-specialize in a given aspect of a Discipline).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because God forbid a White Wolf product ever have sensible formatting or indexing, it's on page 234 under the blood bond. Don't ask me why it's there and not the actually relevant sections, why those sections don't at least include page references, or why there isn't a page reference in the index, I haven't the foggiest idea. </div> </div> </div>For someone that's engaging in ad hominem snark about other people being &quot;oversensitive&quot; this is a pretty rich reaction for being wrong about something.<br /> <br /> You could have just said, &quot;Oops, it wasn't where I said it was, and it's fair that you missed it because it's hidden in a spot that doesn't make sense.&quot; Instead it's a whole tirade about editing because you were so confident it was in a specific section.<br /> <br /> That said, I had a friend send me screen caps of pages 233 and 234. I'm curious where animals being blood bonded or ghouled are mentioned exactly... because I'm staring at the text (admittedly possibly something that's been errataed in a newer printing) and there's no mention of it in your revised section reference.<br /> <br /> I didn't ask you to explain the editing. I asked you for a quotation from the text (since you're asserting a positive that it's there, I can't quote it not being there if I just re-type a section that could be the wrong one). So far you've just offered two page references that don't seem to back up your claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's down to how you interpret the power,... </div> </div> </div>That's not doing it any favors in the &quot;Animalism is underrated because it's too vague, but V5 fixed it&quot; issue... since apparently the V5 version of Animal Succulence is more subject to ST fiat than the V20 version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...thanks to how strangely it's written. </div> </div> </div>That's a stretch. It could certainly be written more clearly... but there isn't an specifically weird writing I can see.<br /> <br /> You increase Hunger slaked when feeding from animals by 1. Your treat your Blood Potency as 2 lower for restrictions on feeding from animals.<br /> <br /> The Blood Potency chart is phrased clearly: At BP 2 (4 for Animal Succulence users) slakes from animal feedings are halved. At BP 3+ (5+ for the power) you cannot slake from animals at all.<br /> <br /> Animal Succulence doesn't say it overrides the BP chart beyond where you fall on it. This isn't an order of operations issue, as the order of operations seem pretty clear: calculate Hunger slaked, add 1, apply the chart (halve or nullify completely if BP is too high). If you were always going to be able to get at least 1 Hunger slaked from animals... the power really should say that.<br /> <br /> If you want to run it otherwise, you can certainly make the case... but again... that's just another hole in the argument that V5 Animalism &quot;fixed&quot; Animalism's perceptions of being underrated because yet again, something could be good, or lackluster, depending on the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now you're just putting words in my mouth. We're now from &quot;V5 did this thing right&quot; to &quot;V5 is the best edition&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Awww... the poor snowflake doesn't like the ad hominem tactics being pointed back at them.<br /> <br /> I told you what made you come off as edition warring, you doubled down on it (and did so more in response), so I'm treating you like the edition warrior you clearly want to be treated as. If you want me to stop, address the actual points, and knock off the snide group-observations-as-personal-slights shit. I will point you to the forum rule 1 about trying to use broad statements about attacking groups to try to hide direct personal attacks as something to consider in your responses (and I check my references, it's there).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People don't consider Serpentis overrated because it provides a lot of <i>overpowered</i> abilities that are capable of replacing entire disciplines, if not being straightforwardly more powerful than entire discipline <i>lines</i>, in a pinch. </div> </div> </div>So... you're conceding that your logic is faulty?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If nobody disagrees with that -- and it doesn't seem like anyone is -- why is it a bone of contention? </div> </div> </div><b>YOU.</b><br /> <br /> You. Literally. Just. Disagreed. With. That.<br /> <br /> You said, &quot;...because it solves for the root issue with Animalism itself: it's a hodgepodge of two themes which don't coexist well...&quot; which is not what I just said the root cause of Animalism is, and you apparently think my assessment is undisputed in this thread... while you're disputing it!<br /> <br /> Your whole premise for saying that V5 Animalism is great, and illustrates why V5 is in general so great you have the right to insult everyone that disagrees while being immune from any social consequences, is that Animalism wasn't underrated because of the lack of clarity of what many of it's powers can really do due to high levels of ST interpretation and variable OOC knowledge of animal behavioral science, but because of thematic incoherence which V5 &quot;fixes&quot; by adding more powers to two separate themes instead.<br /> <br /> You. Are The. Problem. Not the rest of us being whatever buzzword you want to use to say, &quot;everyone else's emotions make them dumb and wrong, but my emotions a sacred and objectively validating of anything I claim is a fact.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T13:21:07-07:00","id":1541078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541058#post1541058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole problem is that your post doesn't address the theme of the thread, but instead just double down on saying V5 did it better in every way. It is gratuitous, and it is this gratuity what's the problem.<br /> <br /> You could say the same thing as a short comment instead of a full tangent, and it would be ok. You could even give an example of V5 build that's less sensitive to ST fiat and it would be 100% within the conversation.<br /> <br /> Heck, I'm about to play in a V5 game, I'd welcome some constructive commentary on what we can do within the game and which powers are underrated in it.<br /> <br /> But all you did was a huge tangent that don't say anything helpful or interesting other than &quot;V5 has the superior version&quot;<br /> <br /> And no, the problem with Animalism isn't by any stretch being a hodgepodge of concepts. That's hardly a unique problem of Animalism. Serpentis isn't that overpowered, by the way, and heck, have you ever paid attention to Presence!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T15:39:43-07:00","id":1541088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541032#post1541032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit of a mixed bag.<br /> <br /> V5 Discipline activation pools generally use an Attribute + Discipline rating rather than a Skill. While Disciplines aren't cheap in V5 (char gen or with XP), you have less overall traits you have to invest in to get as good as you can with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be cheaper in real terms if the overall skills were fewer to the point that 1XP 'buys more' but in V20, there are a relative few skills that are too advantageous to pass up and the rest are flavor or char concept. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What dice pool you &quot;need&quot; depends entirely on what you define as &quot;regularly be proficient,&quot; and how liberal your ST is with taking half </div> </div> </div>Gonna vary slightly table to table but in V20 1 success is a 'win' and 3 a 'strong win'. At difficulty 6. Rough math: 2 dice tends to = 1 success(less so if 1s subtract but im just illustrating the point). That means 6 dice in the pool to be 'above average good' at something at normal circumstances. Diff 7 3 dice += about 1 success, if 8 = 4. So on. <br /> <br /> So IMO, if someone is really good at a task, they should be able to regularly display average or above average competence in un-ideal circumstances. And in V20 with the Dice Pool Splitting mechanic, if your split dice pools synergize(they all have equal values in dots so none are restrictive to the potential pool), then with 8 dice in a pool, a char should be able to output 3+ successes in most situation barring any huge mitigating factors.<br /> <br /> V5 i think(unless it has changed) you can spend a WP for 3 extra dice(about one success?) or &quot;win at a cost&quot; which will really depend upon the ST. im not sure how 'Taking Half' works or could be exploited.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, thankfully, as Animal Succulence would be completely worthless if you had to make Rouse checks to feed off of animals for a bit longer than normal as your Blood Potency increases. That said, V5 Animalism is rather Rouse heavy with only two core powers that don't require checks. Though the three checks to use Bond Famulus last until the animal dies, and negates the Rouse checks of two of the higher level powers you're going to want to use on them a lot; so it's a large net savings for your one close animal companion compared to ordering around random creatures. </div> </div> </div>V5 Feral Whispers has a cost of 1 Rouse per animal type, per scene. That, <i>could</i>, get expensive over a night. V20 i dont remember lvls 1-5 having a cost, though for 4/5 you may likely want to spend a WP for an auto success. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really? As far as I can tell the Bond Famulus power is the only one that seems inspired by Requiem directly instead of being a power VtM and VtR have both used at some point previously. Though I think most people would prefer the VtR 2e version of that power over the V5 version given the respective contexts (esp. given the point of the thread VtR 2e's Raise the Familiar explicitly makes that animal as intelligent as an Intelligence 1 human when it comes to understanding orders given, cutting through a lot of the &quot;what can it do exactly?&quot; issues discussed in the thread even if VtR 2e Animalism in general doesn't fully get rid of that problem either). </div> </div> </div>I dont remember but im pretty sure ive only played VtR 1e. <br /> <br /> As far as animal intelligence, that would be a difficult one to ever properly define given the subject matter. I view it in one of 2 ways:<br /> <br /> A.The blood is the intelligent force<br /> B. The animal is the intelligent force <br /> <br /> A is easier but can be ham-fisted with a bad ST. B is far more subject to interpretation and ST/PCs would need some study reference. Example: studies on Crows/Ravens show them to be far more intelligent than previously thought. Perhaps closer to a 7 year old child in some problem solving aspects. Plus, they recognize individual humans and can pass that info along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T16:00:56-07:00","id":1541090,"title":"","content":"In almost all editions/variations of Vampire, B is the stated way Animalism works. My point about Raise the Familiar is that one of its major perks is that it swaps to A. Your animal blood familiar sacrifices some of its instincts (but not natural capabilities) in exchange for supernatural intelligence that makes it much more valuable as a reliable servant. It's not impressive intelligence, but an order like, &quot;Keep the haven safe while I'm out,&quot; will be understood in both the wording and spirit of your intentions because the blood is taking over instead of the animal's brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T17:01:28-07:00","id":1541093,"title":"","content":"As a matter of fact, studies having been showing for a time that pretty much every animal is smarter than previously thought, even insects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T17:06:44-07:00","id":1541095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541093#post1541093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a matter of fact, studies having been showing for a time that pretty much every animal is smarter than previously thought, even insects.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gamer friends are pretty big nature and martial arts buffs. Bunch of nerds and I miss them. <br /> <br /> We got into arguments over essentially National Geographic stuff. I miss those times. <br /> <br /> There are funny vids out there if racoons figuring out how to get under a garage door and also get bait from a live trap without entering it. <br /> <br /> There's a good YouTube vid of a crow solving a seven(?) step puzzle and it has to use tools to get a treat. One involved water displacement. That places at least that crow above the intelligence of many of my coworkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T19:21:07-07:00","id":1541101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541095#post1541095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a good YouTube vid of a crow solving a seven(?) step puzzle and it has to use tools to get a treat. One involved water displacement. That places at least that crow above the intelligence of many of my coworkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think around 75% of characters back in the day were just reskins of Eric Draven from &quot;The Crow&quot; with Brandon Lee from back in 1994. So using a smart animal companion fits in a VtM game. Oh I feel old now....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T03:43:02-07:00","id":1541118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541093#post1541093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a matter of fact, studies having been showing for a time that pretty much every animal is smarter than previously thought, even insects.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a significant problem where science doesn't really have a good definition of intelligence; especially in the light of trying to isolate why humans can do so many things other animals can't (even with training from us) even though our brains aren't really better.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is that what makes humans so &quot;intelligent&quot; is that compared to most animals we're obnoxiously slow to figure things out. The difference between &quot;smart&quot; and &quot;intelligent' might really come down to being extremely slow in cognitive processing, integration, and application. Since we have to spend way more brain power to figure things out, we spend more time thinking about things... which is likely the reason why we end up as a species accomplishing so many feats of intelligence; we have to understand concepts in more depth rather than quickly assimilating stimuli into rapid responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T14:58:33-07:00","id":1541140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541118#post1541118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a significant problem where science doesn't really have a good definition of intelligence; especially in the light of trying to isolate why humans can do so many things other animals can't (even with training from us) even though our brains aren't really better.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is that what makes humans so &quot;intelligent&quot; is that compared to most animals we're obnoxiously slow to figure things out. The difference between &quot;smart&quot; and &quot;intelligent' might really come down to being extremely slow in cognitive processing, integration, and application. Since we have to spend way more brain power to figure things out, we spend more time thinking about things... which is likely the reason why we end up as a species accomplishing so many feats of intelligence; we have to understand concepts in more depth rather than quickly assimilating stimuli into rapid responses.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the problem that evaluating their abilities through training in controlled conditions is orders of magnitude easier than evaluation through observation of what they can accomplish on their own, for several reasons.<br /> <br /> So our previous assumptions are heavily skewed towards recognizing behavior that benefits us, while ignoring things that don't concern us in any capacity. That's specially tricky when it comes to make sense of their subjectivity, like how hard and convoluted it was to recognize playful behavior in bees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T16:47:34-07:00","id":1541148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541077#post1541077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're responding to a line of discussion about your claim than V5 Animalism isn't unique in things like having low dice-pools and high difficulties. So I contrasted it with V5 Dominate. For someone that keeps banging on about how great V5 is, you'd think you could recognize something a distinct as V5's whole, &quot;No roll is required against an unprepared mortal,&quot; caveat present in a number of V5 Dominate powers as being unique to V5 and thus not about V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I contrasted both to their V20 counterparts to show the two situations are in outcome the same, whether you're looking at trivially-low target numbers or auto-success rules themselves in the previous editions. Other than that in pre-V5, one has to worry about target number <i>and</i> degrees of success.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly a mark to your favor when your counter-example is a point to the <i>greater</i> degree of triviality in a past edition. Which is, as I said, entirely consistent to V5: difficulties are higher and dice pools are lower all around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [quote[Such as?[/quote]<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/Animalism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/_fs-ch-1T1wmsGaOgGaSxcX/assets/errorIcon.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/Animalism\" target=\"_blank\"> Client Challenge </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/Animalism\" target=\"_blank\"> https://vtm.paradoxwikis.com/Animalism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Love 'em or hate 'em, Paradox does a wonderful job actually keeping their free wiki up to date with published materials.<br /> <br /> In level 1, we have the &quot;animal&quot; power bond famulus and the &quot;beast&quot; power sense the beast. In level 2, we have animal messenger and feral whispers for &quot;animals&quot;, and atavism which works for both. In level 3, we have messenger's command, animal succulence, plague of beasts, and unliving hive for &quot;animals&quot;; quell the beast for &quot;beast&quot;; bugger me if I know how to categorize scent of prey (but if I had to, I'd put it more in beast). In level 4, we have subsume the spirit and sway the flock for &quot;animals&quot;. In level 5, we have animal dominion for &quot;animals&quot;, and coax the bestial temper and drawing out the beast for &quot;beast&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, there's not yet a Beast-specific power for...Animalism 4. Animalism ruined forever and V5 is the worst TTRPG ever published, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> ...amalgams... </div> </div> </div>Of which there are only three: the two famulus powers, and unliving hive. Unliving hive being the only one out of reach of a starting-level character, with predator type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> For someone that's engaging in ad hominem snark about other people being &quot;oversensitive&quot; this is a pretty rich reaction for being wrong about something. </div> </div> </div>We'll get back to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> You could have just said, &quot;Oops, it wasn't where I said it was, and it's fair that you missed it because it's hidden in a spot that doesn't make sense.&quot; Instead it's a whole tirade about editing because you were so confident it was in a specific section.<br /> <br /> That said, I had a friend send me screen caps of pages 233 and 234. I'm curious where animals being blood bonded or ghouled are mentioned exactly... because I'm staring at the text (admittedly possibly something that's been errataed in a newer printing) and there's no mention of it in your revised section reference. </div> </div> </div><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1657_1724887578936_575\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1657\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1657\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1657&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> That <i><b>is</b></i> the section on ghouls. You can tell by the red bold text separated by line breaks that says &quot;Ghouls&quot;. Relevant text being,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V5 corebook, page 234</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A mortal <i><b>or animal</b></i> who drinks a vampire\u2019s Blood becomes something both more and less than what they were, for a time. Derisively called a ghoul by western vampires\u200b<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> A Rouse Check\u2019s worth of vitae bestows the following benefits to a mortal <i><b>or animal</b></i> for approximately a month...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I asked you for a quotation from the text (since you're asserting a positive that it's there, I can't quote it not being there if I just re-type a section that could be the wrong one). So far you've just offered two page references that don't seem to back up your claim. </div> </div> </div>Well now you have it. Happy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> That's not doing it any favors in the &quot;Animalism is underrated because it's too vague, but V5 fixed it&quot; issue... since apparently the V5 version of Animal Succulence is more subject to ST fiat than the V20 version. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in VtM corebooks universally overrules PEBMAS, and never has it been the case anything in VtM corebooks universally overrule PEBMAS. Again, specific overrides general, and we do see specific case examples where individual powers <i>do</i> overrule PEBMAS (Toughness). If the inverse were the case, there would be no need to explain order of operations for Toughness as it would be a <i>general</i> rule to apply additive changes before multiplicative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> If you were always going to be able to get at least 1 Hunger slaked from animals... the power really should say that. </div> </div> </div>I agree it absolutely should, because there are way too many players out there who aren't considering order of operations and the implication that has for the power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Awww... the poor snowflake doesn't like the ad hominem tactics being pointed back at them....I told you what made you come off as edition warring, you doubled down on it (and did so more in response), so I'm treating you like the edition warrior you clearly want to be treated as. If you want me to stop, address the actual points, and knock off the snide group-observations-as-personal-slights shit. I will point you to the forum rule 1 about trying to use broad statements about attacking groups to try to hide direct personal attacks as something to consider in your responses (and I check my references, it's there).<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Your whole premise for saying that V5 Animalism is great, and illustrates why V5 is in general so great you have the right to insult everyone that disagrees while being immune from any social consequences, is that Animalism wasn't underrated because of the lack of clarity of what many of it's powers can really do due to high levels of ST interpretation and variable OOC knowledge of animal behavioral science, but because of thematic incoherence which V5 &quot;fixes&quot; by adding more powers to two separate themes instead.<br /> <br /> You. Are The. Problem. Not the rest of us being whatever buzzword you want to use to say, &quot;everyone else's emotions make them dumb and wrong, but my emotions a sacred and objectively validating of anything I claim is a fact.&quot;\u200b<br /> </div> </div> </div>Now we get back to in what I put a pin earlier.<br /> <br /> We went from me saying I thought V5 Animalism is an example of V5 mechanics doing a discipline right...to me claiming V5 is the best edition, and edition warring...and now, to me being the problem? <i>I'm</i> the one using ad homs when I said people are letting their biases get the best of them on mere mention of V5?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> So... you're conceding that your logic is faulty? </div> </div> </div>Well I wasn't going to do this, but as you won't drop it...<br /> <br /> The thing is, for your counterexample to hold weight, Serpentis really does have to be a hodgepodge of conflicting themes parallel to Animalism. It's not, Serpentis' theme is &quot;be Thulsa Doom from Conan the Barbarian&quot;. A stupid and racist theme, is still a theme.<br /> <br /> From there that Serpentis is a collection of overpowered discipline powers is a rather academic argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> You said, &quot;...because it solves for the root issue with Animalism itself: it's a hodgepodge of two themes which don't coexist well...&quot; which is not what I just said the root cause of Animalism is, and you apparently think my assessment is undisputed in this thread... while you're disputing it! </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, how silly of me for failing to note the chasm of distinction between &quot;it's too open-ended (because it has conflicting themes and has to cover too much ground) and reliant on ST fiat&quot;, and &quot;it's too vague (for completely unexplained reasons) and reliant on ST fiat&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think you're angry I mentioned V5 in a remotely positive light, and for that reason are hellbound to interpret anything I say in the worst-possible faith out of contrarianism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T20:35:32-07:00","id":1541163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540216-underrated-disciplines-and-why?p=1541148#post1541148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I'm</i> the one using ad homs when I said people are letting their biases get the best of them on mere mention of V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That is the defini